      "message": "A few things of note:\n1. W/o the changes to MtlUtils, GMs that only contain convex shapes would only want a depth attachment, which was then returning false from that function and we\u0027d then error out of the RenderPassTask.\n2. I noticed a few visual discrepancies after this patch, but after fixing #1, I believe it\u0027s not issues with the per-draw logic, but that the current use of std::sort() is not a stable sort. Since nothing writes out the correct depth value, if the sort isn\u0027t stable, we can end up drawing opaque things out of order and get incorrect results.\n\nWith depth-writing being on the table this week, I should be able to confirm that, and if need be, come back to debugging this step.",
